\f0\fs24 \cf0 Aisha Lashari | Academic Coordinator & Chief Advisor, WMwrites\
\
Aisha Lashari is an English language educator, academic leader, public speaking trainer, and debate adjudicator with six years of teaching experience. She currently serves as the Academic Coordinator of O Levels at The City School, Jinnah Campus, Hyderabad. She holds a BS in English with a specialisation in Applied Linguistics from the University of Sindh, Jamshoro, where she ranked at the top of her class for four consecutive years.\
\
A Cambridge-certified O Level and A Level English instructor, Aisha has extensive experience in academic coordination, curriculum implementation, student leadership, debating, and communication training. She is an alumna of the Pakistan-U.S. Alumni Network, a certified English Access MicroScholarship Program and English Works! teacher, an American English Live Series 17 Ambassador, and a participant in the Professional Development for Global Classrooms (PGCC) 2025 programme. She has also led educational initiatives, including the ChangeX SDG Conference 2026, and mentored students in debating and Model United Nations.\
\
As Chief Advisor of WMwrites, Aisha envisions building a community where young writers find their authentic voices, express ideas with confidence, and engage thoughtfully with the world. She believes writing is more than an academic skill; it is a means of self-expression, empathy, and meaningful change. Through mentorship and creative exploration, she hopes to nurture thoughtful, articulate, and socially conscious individuals who understand the power and responsibility of words.}